- `action(n1, "start the purchase process")`: Hallucinated step; the source begins directly with "make a purchase" without any introductory action.
- `precedence(i1, n1)` and `precedence(n1, n2)`: Violates exact chronology by inserting an unrequested node at the start, contradicting the source's opening statement.
- `defines(v1, "add items to cart?", {})`: Variable range is empty `{}`; fails to capture the binary decision space implied by "choose to 'Add Items to cart'" versus "decide not to add items".
- `branch(b1, XOR)`: Lacks corresponding `guard` statements to specify conditions on outgoing edges based on `v1`, omitting the conditional routing logic described in the source.
- `action(n7, "End of process")` and `action(n9, "End of process")`: Redundant action nodes placed immediately before terminal `end` nodes; the source simply states "the process will end" without defining an intermediate action step.
- `actor(a_default, "Default", [...])`: Participant name "Default" misrepresents the responsible actor explicitly identified in the source as "the customer".

Structural Check
- [S1] STC11 failed: Each variable definition must have a valid range with at least two distinct values. | Variable `v1` has an invalid range `[]`.
- [S2] STC16 failed: Every outgoing edge of XOR/OR branches must have exactly one guard. | XOR/OR edge `b1 -> n6` has 0 guards; exactly one is required. | XOR/OR edge `b1 -> n8` has 0 guards; exactly one is required.